WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.955
Operational security begins with protecting the workstation itself.

00:00:03.955 --> 00:00:07.000
Apply operating-system, browser, application, and extension updates.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:10.820
Use supported endpoint protection, a host firewall, screen locking,

00:00:10.820 --> 00:00:14.000
and physical safeguards appropriate to the sensitivity of the work.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:18.130
Use unique passwords stored in an approved password manager and enable multi-factor

00:00:18.130 --> 00:00:19.930
authentication where available.

00:00:19.930 --> 00:00:21.990
Recovery methods should be controlled and documented.

00:00:21.990 --> 00:00:24.000
Do not place case credentials, API keys,

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:26.883
or sensitive notes in browser scripts or unprotected files.

00:00:26.883 --> 00:00:31.515
A VPN can protect traffic on untrusted networks and provide an approved organizational

00:00:31.515 --> 00:00:32.000
connection,

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:35.950
but it does not guarantee anonymity or make prohibited activity acceptable.

00:00:35.950 --> 00:00:39.000
Providers and destinations may still log information.

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:42.595
Choose and use network services according to policy and the investigation's legitimate

00:00:42.595 --> 00:00:42.990
need.

00:00:42.990 --> 00:00:47.275
Separate personal accounts and identifiers from research workflows to reduce contamination

00:00:47.275 --> 00:00:48.930
and accidental disclosure.

00:00:48.930 --> 00:00:52.255
This is basic compartmentation, not permission to impersonate people,

00:00:52.255 --> 00:00:55.000
create deceptive access, or enter private communities.

00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:56.990
Minimize unnecessary exposure.

00:00:56.990 --> 00:01:01.000
Collect only what the requirement needs, avoid publishing sensitive findings broadly,

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:03.180
and restrict case material to authorized users.

00:01:03.180 --> 00:01:06.000
Public information can still create privacy, safety,

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:08.930
and reputational harm when aggregated or mishandled.

00:01:08.930 --> 00:01:10.990
Legal and ethical boundaries govern the workstation.

00:01:10.990 --> 00:01:15.898
Do not bypass access controls, use stolen credentials, harass, doxx, stalk,

00:01:15.898 --> 00:01:17.000
or conduct unlawful surveillance.

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:21.980
When authority is unclear, pause and seek policy, privacy, legal, or supervisory review.
